Alembic owns PostgreSQL schema changes. API startup does not create tables.

Apply migrations locally (uses .env):
    uv run alembic upgrade head

Apply migrations using the Docker environment:
    docker compose build api
    docker compose run --rm api /app/.venv/bin/alembic upgrade head
    docker compose up -d api

Create a migration after changing models:
    uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
Review the generated migration before applying it. Autogeneration is a draft;
it cannot infer data transformations or renamed columns safely.

Check schema alignment:
    uv run alembic check

Revision 0001 describes the legacy create_all schema. The inspected existing
local database was stamped at 0001 before applying 0002. For new empty databases,
run upgrade head without stamping. Never stamp a schema that does not match.

Revision 0002 deletes ALL task and user records before changing integer user IDs
to WorkOS string IDs and adding the foreign key. This was authorized only for
this disposable development database. It must not be used on a database with
data to preserve. Downgrade from 0002 is deliberately unsupported because
WorkOS IDs cannot be converted back to meaningful integer identities.
